WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.060 --> 00:00:06.430
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie and This is going
to be my Constantine Review.

00:00:06.430 --> 00:00:09.809
The episode they aired was actually a slightly
different version from the original pilot.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:14.580
They made a few changes to the cast, all good
things.

00:00:14.580 --> 00:00:19.529
I’ll totally explain what’s going on as
I work through best moments.

00:00:19.529 --> 00:00:22.089
I will be doing weekly videos for all the
episodes.

00:00:22.089 --> 00:00:24.210
So be sure to subscribe to get everything.

00:00:24.210 --> 00:00:27.740
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
it yet, starting with Top 5 moment,

00:00:27.740 --> 00:00:30.409
Number 5 - Ravenscar Psychiatric Hospital

00:00:30.409 --> 00:00:36.020
This is the place Constantine admits himself
to after Astra was taken to Hell.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:38.920
In the comics he’s been in and out of it
more than once, but on the show I don’t

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:40.000
think they’ll send him back.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.250
Or if they do it would be at the end of the
season and then at the beginning of season

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:44.250
2 he’d leave again.

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:45.250
It’s a place they could go back to.

00:00:45.250 --> 00:00:46.250
But I don’t think they will.

00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:49.570
They changed a few things about the Astra
incident on the show too.

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:55.600
In the comics, Constantine had his own Punk
Rock band called Mucous Membrane in the early

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:56.600
80s.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:00.500
While they were playing in Newcastle England
they found a girl named Astra who had raised

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:05.070
a demon to get revenge on a group of people
that had been sexually abusing her.

00:01:05.070 --> 00:01:07.840
The rest of the story is pretty much what
the show told.

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:11.899
Constantine tried to raise his own demon to
destroy Astra’s demon but he lost control

00:01:11.899 --> 00:01:12.899
of it.

00:01:12.899 --> 00:01:22.969
The demon killed Astra’s lesser demon and
then killed her, taking her soul to hell.

00:01:22.969 --> 00:01:30.000
She’s currently being held hostage by the
Demon Nergal, he’s one of the big inner

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:31.210
circle demons they mentioned.

00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:37.200
In the comics, he’s like Constantine’s
Moriarty, his biggest nemesis.

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:44.229
So Nergal is the big bad on the show.

00:01:44.229 --> 00:01:54.899
Number 4 - Liv Aberdeen, Jasper Winters and
the Zed Swap

00:01:54.899 --> 00:02:02.990
Liv Aberdeen wasn’t from the comics, she
was a new character they created for the show.

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:07.310
NBC and the producers just decided the character
wasn’t working so they reshot some things

00:02:07.310 --> 00:02:09.080
from the pilot and during the episode we just
watched.

00:02:09.080 --> 00:02:11.409
They added the scene at the end with the woman
drawing all the pictures.

00:02:11.409 --> 00:02:15.180
If you couldn’t tell, those were illustrations
from the comics, just a nice nod to some of

00:02:15.180 --> 00:02:16.180
the more famous Hellblazer stories.

00:02:16.180 --> 00:02:22.590
Her name is Zed, she’s a comic book character
and will be in all the episodes going forward.

00:02:22.590 --> 00:02:24.879
She’s the new female lead.

00:02:24.879 --> 00:02:26.420
The Liv character probably isn’t coming
back.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:30.209
I know it sounds weird, but it would have
been too expensive for them to reshoot the

00:02:30.209 --> 00:02:31.209
pilot.

00:02:31.209 --> 00:02:36.610
I’m a huge fan of Lucy Griffiths but all
of the changes they made to the show are for

00:02:36.610 --> 00:02:38.880
the better.

00:02:38.880 --> 00:02:40.670
You guys will totally dig the Zed character.

00:02:40.670 --> 00:02:42.629
She’s being played by Anjelica Celaya.

00:02:42.629 --> 00:02:46.340
They even brought her to Comic Con this summer.

00:02:46.340 --> 00:02:49.830
What they are keeping is Jasper Winter’s
Tower and the scryers map Liv made.

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:57.510
That will be the device that they use to travel
from mystery to mystery as they help people

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:03.590
and try to figure out what Nergal is trying
to do on earth.

00:03:03.590 --> 00:03:09.099
The tower itself works a lot like the Tower
of Fate, but it’s not the Tower of Fate.

00:03:09.099 --> 00:03:12.621
Even though they had the helmet of fate in
there.

00:03:12.621 --> 00:03:17.489
And I know a lot of you were asking me whether
the skull in the glass case meant Pandora

00:03:17.489 --> 00:03:19.239
would be coming on the show.

00:03:19.239 --> 00:03:25.129
At comic con David Goyer said that the show
had free reign in the mystical corner of the

00:03:25.129 --> 00:03:30.849
DC Universe, so potentially they could do
a version of Justice League Dark at some point.

00:03:30.849 --> 00:03:34.030
They can do any of the mystical characters
they want.

00:03:34.030 --> 00:03:35.650
So everyone is up for grabs.

00:03:35.650 --> 00:03:39.980
But don’t expect Doctor Fate, That would
be like bringing Superman on Arrow.

00:03:39.980 --> 00:03:41.989
Speaking of supporting characters.

00:03:41.989 --> 00:03:44.349
Number 3 - Team Constantine

00:03:44.349 --> 00:03:49.150
So right now here’s who the good guys are
going to be.

00:03:49.150 --> 00:03:55.109
John Constantine of course, Chaz and Zed from
the comics and Manny the Angel.

00:03:55.109 --> 00:04:00.569
He’s not from the comics but Constantine
has worked with angels in the past.

00:04:00.569 --> 00:04:04.810
If you picked up the antagonistic vibe from
Constantine when Manny started poking in his

00:04:04.810 --> 00:04:09.930
business it’s because he generally holds
all of heaven and all of hell in contempt.

00:04:09.930 --> 00:04:14.290
He hates everyone, but like Manny teased,
if he can help Heaven stop whatever Nergal

00:04:14.290 --> 00:04:16.380
is planning, it might redeem his soul.

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:19.480
They damned him to hell when Astra’s soul
was taken by Nergal.

00:04:19.480 --> 00:04:23.440
As for potential other characters this season,
they’ll probably start making more announcements

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:26.270
once the show gets picked up for a full season.

00:04:26.270 --> 00:04:29.110
We probably won’t learn about that for a
couple weeks.

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:33.850
But because Warner Brothers wants to flex
it’s tv muscles as much as possible, I think

00:04:33.850 --> 00:04:37.080
the odds the show will be safe from cancellation
are pretty good.

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:42.970
The other supporting characters in the episode
weren’t necessarily allies but I’ll explain

00:04:42.970 --> 00:04:45.819
them when I do more easter eggs in a sec.

00:04:45.819 --> 00:04:47.410
Number 2 - The Demon Nergal

00:04:47.410 --> 00:04:52.610
They teased him as the big bad but he’s
the biggest villain Constantine has dealt

00:04:52.610 --> 00:04:54.900
with on a regular basis in the comics.

00:04:54.900 --> 00:04:58.650
He really only started dealing with Satan
directly during the Dangerous Habits Storyline.

00:04:58.650 --> 00:05:01.440
That’s also the comic that deals with him
having terminal cancer.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:05.599
The show isn’t doing this, mostly because
he can’t smoke on tv.

00:05:05.599 --> 00:05:14.979
The lighter that he keeps flipping during
the episode is a reference to that.

00:05:14.979 --> 00:05:21.930
I don’t think Satan will be a notable character
on the show this season, I think Nergal will

00:05:21.930 --> 00:05:33.039
be the biggest villain we meet.

00:05:33.039 --> 00:05:35.639
Number 1 - Dark Constantine

00:05:35.639 --> 00:05:40.360
In the comics Constantine had to face an evil
future version of himself and there was even

00:05:40.360 --> 00:05:44.070
a brief period when he was forced to let Nergal
possess his body.

00:05:44.070 --> 00:05:47.190
On the show this big scene at the end was
one of the things they changed from the original

00:05:47.190 --> 00:05:48.190
pilot.

00:05:48.190 --> 00:05:49.190
I guess just because they thought it worked
better thematically than having a random demon.

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:52.530
I did see the original pilot and I have to
agree that Dark Constantine is way better.

00:05:52.530 --> 00:05:55.360
Expect the show to use him again as a villain
device.

00:05:55.360 --> 00:06:00.010
It just seems like too much fun to have your
hero fighting an evil future version of himself.

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:06.990
It’s almost like the Flash with Professor
Zoom being a future twisted version of a speedster.

00:06:06.990 --> 00:06:10.220
Let me know what your favorite moment was,
and while you think about it.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:12.770
Here’s all the other easter eggs I spotted:

00:06:12.770 --> 00:06:18.180
So I already mentioned the Helmet of Fate,
but Jasper Winters on the show might be Baron

00:06:18.180 --> 00:06:19.180
Winters.

00:06:19.180 --> 00:06:24.009
In the comics he was the host for all souls
not claimed by Heaven or Hell.

00:06:24.009 --> 00:06:26.069
So he went mad from it all.

00:06:26.069 --> 00:06:29.819
But he did live in an alternate dimension,
so you could think of the tower they’re

00:06:29.819 --> 00:06:32.050
using as their home base as that place.

00:06:32.050 --> 00:06:38.690
Here’s the Ibistick, it’s a magical wand
that can be used for acts of good.

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:47.270
It works a little like the helmet of fate
in that when someone uses it it bonds with

00:06:47.270 --> 00:06:48.270
them.

00:06:48.270 --> 00:06:51.650
But it doesn’t work against black magic
which is an interesting twist.

00:06:51.650 --> 00:06:56.139
Ibis is connected to the Shazam family, but
since the movies are doing Shazam and Black

00:06:56.139 --> 00:06:57.139
Adam.

00:06:57.139 --> 00:06:58.690
I don’t expect them to appear on the show.

00:06:58.690 --> 00:07:02.060
Then there’s Pandora’s Box, this is the
skull of Pandora, the biblical pandora who

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:03.479
unleashed all evil into the world.

00:07:03.479 --> 00:07:07.919
The Doctor John meets with here, Doctor Huntoon
also worked at Arkham Asylum.

00:07:07.919 --> 00:07:11.620
In the comics he also ended up trying to hurt
constantine for wrecking his personal life.

00:07:11.620 --> 00:07:17.180
If the show doesn’t go back to Ravenscar
then I don’t expect that character to come

00:07:17.180 --> 00:07:18.830
back very often.

00:07:18.830 --> 00:07:22.090
Ritchie Simpson in the comics ended up becoming
a techno demon.

00:07:22.090 --> 00:07:26.039
I don’t know if they’ll keep using his
character, but these toy robots on his desk

00:07:26.039 --> 00:07:28.440
are a big wink at his future.

00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:34.319
Ivy University where he works is also the
same place in the comics where the Ray Palmer

00:07:34.319 --> 00:07:39.229
Atom was a professor, it’s also the place
where the Ronnie Raymond Firestorm was a student.

00:07:39.229 --> 00:07:43.119
Both Arrow and the Flash are doing those characters,
so it’s a nice link up with those shows.

00:07:43.119 --> 00:07:47.509
The backwards writing on the wall here might
be an easter egg for Zatanna or Zatarra.

00:07:47.509 --> 00:07:51.259
Both characters have been on TV before so
Constantine could totally bring them on too

00:07:51.259 --> 00:07:52.259
at some point.

00:07:52.259 --> 00:07:54.120
Let me know if you spotted any other references
I didn’t mention.

00:07:54.120 --> 00:07:57.189
And to answer the big crossover question.

00:07:57.189 --> 00:08:00.639
Yes, Constantine does exist inside the shared
DC TV show universe.

00:08:00.639 --> 00:08:01.639
But because it’s a different network, don’t
expect to see stephen amell or grant gustin

00:08:01.639 --> 00:08:02.639
cameo any time soon.

00:08:02.639 --> 00:08:03.639
But yes, they are connected.

00:08:03.639 --> 00:08:06.699
Overall I gave the episode a solid B. Generally
I don’t get as excited for Pilot episodes

00:08:06.699 --> 00:08:10.849
as I do for the regular series.

00:08:10.849 --> 00:08:16.099
Pilots are designed to jam everything and
the kitchen sink into a 42 minute window.

00:08:16.099 --> 00:08:21.720
Normal episodes keep things much simpler so
you get to spend more time developing a few

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:22.720
characters versus many.

00:08:22.720 --> 00:08:27.159
So just in general, expect the show to be
a lot more fun once as we see more and more

00:08:27.159 --> 00:08:28.159
new episodes.

00:08:28.159 --> 00:08:32.190
New shows in general always have a really
easy time getting better.

00:08:32.190 --> 00:08:38.649
It always takes a while to figure out the
characters from a writing standpoint.

00:08:38.649 --> 00:08:46.899
I am a fan of Matt Ryan’s very British Constantine,
I’m so glad the show got that right.

00:08:46.899 --> 00:08:51.600
Harold Perrineau is great and I love his stuff
so I’m interested to see more of Manny.

00:08:51.600 --> 00:09:02.060
He didn’t have a lot of time in the pilot
so it’s hard to get a sense of his character.

00:09:02.060 --> 00:09:04.280
The same is true of Charles Halford as Chas.

00:09:04.280 --> 00:09:08.610
Another huge character from the comics, so
I’m excited to watch the actor develop him.

00:09:08.610 --> 00:09:14.290
Zed we haven’t really seen yet, so I can’t
say much about her.

00:09:14.290 --> 00:09:16.620
She’ll be in next week’s episode.

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:23.570
In general the story was great, I didn’t
mind the minor changes to his backstory.

00:09:23.570 --> 00:09:38.390
As long as they throw us a swamp thing bone
every once and a while.

00:09:38.390 --> 00:09:41.040
I’ll post my episode 2 review after next
week’s episode airs.

00:09:41.040 --> 00:09:47.839
I won’t be doing a q&amp;a for this just because
I’m already doing a bunch of videos tomorrow.

00:09:47.839 --> 00:09:51.200
But I’ll try to answer as many questions
as possible in the comments.

00:09:51.200 --> 00:09:56.370
Right now click here to learn more about my
favorite Constantine Comic Stories and Click

00:09:56.370 --> 00:09:57.649
here for this week’s Arrow.

00:09:57.649 --> 00:09:59.999
Thanks for watching, now let’s all high
five and I’ll see you guys tomorrow!

